{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured node2 to synchronize `/etc/inventory/app.conf` atomically from node1 every five minutes. Automatic propagation was demonstrated in 41 seconds. Both nodes were restarted sequentially and fully recovered with matching configuration hash `ea6c7835…b220e5`.","actions_performed":["Created the initially absent canonical configuration file on node1.","Generated a dedicated node2 SSH key restricted on node1 to exporting only the inventory configuration.","Installed and enabled a persistent systemd synchronization service and timer on node2.","Verified automatic change propagation, then removed the test probe and restored the clean synchronized state.","Restarted node1 and node2 individually, proving changed boot identities and post-restart recovery."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Node1 is the source of truth and node2 maintains an atomic synchronized copy","command_ids":["cmd-c2919b94ac8c4411","cmd-8cf247dd39c34032","cmd-664119f2517a482a"],"summary":"Shows the canonical source, restricted export path, successful initial copy, matching hash, and enabled five-minute timer."},{"requirement":"Changes are picked up within 15 minutes","command_ids":["cmd-7272ca72f50f46c2","cmd-cc8c3373089f4b35"],"summary":"A timestamped node1 mutation at 09:56:04 appeared automatically on node2 with identical content and hash by 09:56:45."},{"requirement":"Node1 restart persistence and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-49b023da67d9485b","cmd-aee5cd271cbc4494","cmd-16175bebeec64c81","cmd-c2d23d98d37e4556"],"summary":"Captures healthy baseline boot ID, restart acknowledgement, changed boot ID, and recovered SSH service and source data."},{"requirement":"Node2 restart persistence and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-ac0f5453410e4a8c","cmd-2a2aa4d986c54b13","cmd-0c923dbe10d54086","cmd-9b9df92002e34885","cmd-43d7860c5cbd4301"],"summary":"Captures healthy baseline, restart acknowledgement, changed boot ID, recovered enabled/active timer, successful synchronization, p